  "cause": "The native shared typed lookup now retains complete single-field record-array owner views, but those views never reached the existing table descriptor/consumer projection. Four additional owners coexist with older exact raw LONG parent declarations; native admission retains the raw unit as field_type=long, which is presentation rather than a scalar-table contract.",
  "implementation": [
    "Project already validated pointer-record views into existing native pointer descriptors with structured_range count proof. Preserve all canonical leaf items, target domains, references and parent aliases. No raw pointer scan, new ownership model or game-specific name/address rule.",
    "The existing shared indexed-base consumer walk then observes the newly exposed collections and projects its existing address expressions. No new table-shaped instruction recognizer.",
    "A raw parent is compatible only as raw storage: exact root/start/extent and matching raw unit, no struct/field/pointer/target/semantic table contract. Explicit scalar tables, mixed pointer domains, missing members, code crossings and incompatible overlaps still refuse. The same fixture reproduced the raw-unit mismatch before repair.",
    "Optional native profile lists each candidate and admission reason. The audit joins native collection consumers by exact table section/start/end while retaining their instruction section and conditional index evidence."
  ],
